---
const pipeline = [
  "AST-pattern rules",
  "Dependency models",
  "Semantic compilation",
  "Fixpoint analysis",
  "Finding",
];
---

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="analysis-engine-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">The analysis engine</p>
      <h2 id="analysis-engine-heading" class="section-heading">Fast scans. Fewer false alarms. Fewer missed findings.</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-[66ch] font-mono text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
        OpenTaint makes exhaustive analysis scalable by compressing the search instead of truncating it, then applies explicit security semantics throughout the codebase.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="section-content overflow-hidden border-y border-border-strong bg-background">
      <figcaption class="sr-only">How OpenTaint turns rules and dependency models into an interprocedural finding</figcaption>

      <ol class="engine-pipeline grid border-b border-border-strong sm:grid-cols-5">
        {pipeline.map((step, index) => (
          <li class:list={[
            "relative flex min-h-16 items-center px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-foreground",
            index > 0 && "border-t border-border sm:border-l sm:border-t-0",
            index === pipeline.length - 1 && "text-primary",
          ]}>
            <span class="mr-3 text-primary">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            {step}
            {index < pipeline.length - 1 && <span class="engine-pipeline-pulse absolute bottom-0 left-0 h-px bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="reveal min-w-0 border-b border-border-strong p-6 lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r lg:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-primary">Fast scans</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-mono text-xl font-semibold leading-8 text-foreground">Compress the search</h3>

          <div class="mt-8 border border-border bg-code-header p-4" role="img" aria-label="Related taint states collapse into a compact representation">
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <span class="engine-state block h-2 w-full bg-border-strong"></span>
              <span class="engine-state block h-2 w-[88%] bg-border-strong"></span>
              <span class="engine-state block h-2 w-[72%] bg-border-strong"></span>
              <span class="engine-state block h-2 w-[94%] bg-border-strong"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="my-4 flex items-center gap-3 font-mono text-[9px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-muted-foreground">
              <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border-strong"></span>
              compact representation
              <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border-strong"></span>
            </div>
            <span class="engine-compact block h-5 w-full border border-primary bg-primary/10"></span>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-6 text-muted-foreground">Abductive inference avoids redundant expansion while compact taint languages preserve the complete search space.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="reveal min-w-0 border-b border-border-strong p-6 lg:border-b-0 lg:border-r lg:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-primary">Fewer false alarms</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-mono text-xl font-semibold leading-8 text-foreground">Model the relevant semantics precisely</h3>

          <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden border border-border bg-code-header font-mono text-[10px] leading-6">
            <p class="border-b border-border px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground">graal-eval.yaml</p>
            <p class="px-3 pt-3 text-foreground">Context.eval(..., <span class="bg-primary/15 px-1 text-primary">$UNTRUSTED</span>)</p>
            <p class="px-3 text-primary">focus-metavariable: $UNTRUSTED</p>
            <p class="mt-3 border-t border-border px-3 py-2 text-muted-foreground">Builder.option: this → result</p>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-6 text-muted-foreground">Focused values, structured access paths, and explicit dependency models avoid broad guesses about application and library behavior.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="reveal min-w-0 p-6 lg:p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-primary">Fewer missed findings</p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 font-mono text-xl font-semibold leading-8 text-foreground">Continue until propagation stabilizes</h3>

          <div class="mt-8 border border-border bg-code-header p-4" role="img" aria-label="Analysis continues across calls, fields, aliases, and asynchronous code until fixpoint">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr_auto_1fr_auto_1fr_auto] items-center font-mono text-[8px] text-muted-foreground">
              <span>call</span><span class="engine-depth-rail h-px bg-primary"></span>
              <span>field</span><span class="engine-depth-rail h-px bg-primary"></span>
              <span>alias</span><span class="engine-depth-rail h-px bg-primary"></span>
              <span class="text-primary">fixpoint</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-6 gap-2">
              {Array.from({ length: 18 }).map((_, index) => (
                <span class:list={[
                  "aspect-square border",
                  index % 5 === 0 ? "border-primary bg-primary/15" : "border-border-strong bg-background",
                ]}></span>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-[11px] leading-6 text-muted-foreground">Extended IFDS propagation reaches fixpoint without artificial call-depth, file-depth, or access-path limits.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="grid border-t border-border-strong md:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]">
        <h3 class="border-b border-border-strong px-6 py-6 font-mono text-lg font-semibold leading-8 text-foreground md:border-b-0 md:border-r lg:px-8">Open source, batteries included</h3>
        <p class="px-6 py-6 font-mono text-[11px] leading-6 text-muted-foreground lg:px-8">Engine, AST-pattern rules, dependency models, agent skills, viewer, CLI, and CI integrations ship together under open-source licenses.</p>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .engine-pipeline-pulse {
      width: 38%;
      animation: engine-pipeline 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
    }

    .engine-state {
      animation: engine-state 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
    }

    .engine-state:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 90ms; }
    .engine-state:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 180ms; }
    .engine-state:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 270ms; }

    .engine-compact {
      animation: engine-compact 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
    }

    .engine-depth-rail {
      transform-origin: left;
      animation: engine-depth 3.2s ease-in-out infinite;
    }
  }

  @keyframes engine-pipeline {
    0%, 12% { transform: translateX(-100%); opacity: 0; }
    28%, 68% { transform: translateX(80%); opacity: 1; }
    86%, 100% { transform: translateX(260%); opacity: 0; }
  }

  @keyframes engine-state {
    0%, 18% { transform: translateX(0); opacity: 1; }
    48%, 72% { transform: translateX(6%); opacity: 0.35; }
    100% { transform: translateX(0); opacity: 1; }
  }

  @keyframes engine-compact {
    0%, 28% { opacity: 0.25; transform: scaleX(0.2); transform-origin: left; }
    52%, 84% { opacity: 1; transform: scaleX(1); transform-origin: left; }
    100% { opacity: 0.25; transform: scaleX(0.2); transform-origin: left; }
  }

  @keyframes engine-depth {
    0%, 16% { transform: scaleX(0); opacity: 0.25; }
    58%, 88% { transform: scaleX(1); opacity: 1; }
    100% { transform: scaleX(0); opacity: 0.25; }
  }
</style>
